## The Philosophy of Safe AI

Lani Watson explains that asking questions:
- Is an act of intellectual honesty
- Requires genuine curiosity
- Shows respect for complexity
- Admits uncertainty

This is EXACTLY what safe AI needs.

Not confident answers.
Not bold predictions.
But humble questions.

---

## Practical Example: The Doctor

A doctor with diagnostic AI doesn't want answers.
They want better questions:

✓ "What haven't you considered?"
✓ "Where could this be wrong?"
✓ "What rare pattern could this match?"
✓ "What would change your mind?"

Good AI asks questions.
Bad AI just answers.

